# Appendix A, part 3: environment, other programs, files.
.h2 Environment variables [appcmd-env]
.ix Environment variables
.ix Environment variables, list
These are the environment variables that Strata reads and that a person may
set.  One that is set and empty counts as not set, except where noted.
.h3 Environment variables of Strata [appcmd-env-strata]
.ix STRATA_HOME
.ix STRATA_SPELL
.ix STRATA_THESAURUS
.ix STRATA_TEMPLATES
.ix STRATA_HELP
.ix STRATA_COLORS
.ix STRATA_DEFAULT_COLORS
.ix STRATA_ASCII
.table 17 12 30
Name | Read by | Effect
{c:STRATA_HELP} | Document Manager, Editor | The help file, used after the option
 | | {c:-H} ({n:str-help-search}).
{c:STRATA_COLORS} | Terminal version | The number of colors of the terminal: none, 16,
 | | 256 or truecolor.  It replaces what {c:TERM} and {c:COLORTERM} say
 | | ({n:appterm-colour}).
{c:STRATA_DEFAULT_COLORS} | Document Manager, Editor | When set to anything but
 | | empty or 0, the colors that the program is delivered with replace those
 | | of the settings.  The option {c:--default-colors} does the same.
{c:STRATA_ASCII} | Terminal version | 1 draws the screen with ASCII characters,
 | | 0 with UTF-8, whatever the terminal reports ({n:appterm-charset}).
{c:STRATA_HOME} | Document Manager, Editor | The directory of the settings, instead
 | | of .strata in the home directory.  When it is set, the older settings
 | | file is not read ({n:appcfg}).
{c:STRATA_SPELL} | Editor | The program of the spell check (a full path, or a name
 | | looked up in the fixed system directories), instead of {c:aspell} and then
 | | {c:hunspell}.
{c:STRATA_THESAURUS} | Editor | The directory (or the file) of the thesaurus,
 | | instead of the system directory of the thesaurus data.
{c:STRATA_TEMPLATES} | Editor | A directory searched for a template named in
 | | File, New, after the Working Directory, before the
 | | directory of the program ({n:appcfg-search-templates}).
.end
.if .STRATA_BUILD_TYPE # release
.ix STRATA_LP
.ix STRATA_LPSTAT
.ix SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
.ix STRATA_CTAN_URL
For developers: these environment variables are read as well.
.rows 20 14 36
{c:STRATA_LP} | Editor | The program that sends a PDF to the printer, instead
 | | of {c:lp} ({n:print-sending}).
{c:STRATA_LPSTAT} | Editor | The program that lists the queues, instead of {c:lpstat}.
{c:STRATA_CTAN_URL} | Document Manager | The base address of the font archives,
 | | instead of https://mirrors.ctan.org/install/fonts, for Install Now in
 | | the TeX Font Association (the archive is NAME.tds.zip).
{c:SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH} | Printer | A number of seconds since 1 January 1970.  The
 | | exported LaTeX source names the day of that moment, in UTC, in its first
 | | comment instead of the day of the run ({n:file-export-latex}).
{c:STRATA_LPINFO} | Editor | The program that searches for printers, instead of
 | | {c:lpinfo}, for Search for printers ({n:print-sending}).
{c:STRATA_PROGRAM_DIRS} | all programs | A list of absolute directories, separated by
 | | colons, that is searched for the programs before the system
 | | directories.
{c:STRATA_LPSTAT_REFRESH_MS} | Editor | The time in milliseconds between two reads of
 | | the list of queues while the Print panel is open.
{c:STRATA_X11_DUMP} | X11 version | A file to which the text of the screen is written
 | | after every draw (used by the tests).
{c:STRATA_SCROLL_LOG} | Editor | A file to which each scroll of the text is appended
 | | (used by the tests).
.end
.endif
.h3 Environment variables of the system [appcmd-env-system]
.ix HOME
.ix XDG_CONFIG_HOME
.ix XDG_CACHE_HOME
.ix TMPDIR
.ix PATH
.ix DISPLAY
.ix WAYLAND_DISPLAY
.ix USER
.ix TERM
.ix COLORTERM
.ix LC_ALL
.table 15 12 32
Name | Read by | Effect
{c:HOME} | Document Manager, Editor | The home directory.  If it is empty the home
 | | directory that the system has for the user is used.  The
 | | settings are in the directory .strata of it, and the cache of the
 | | equations is in .cache/strata.
{c:XDG_CONFIG_HOME} | Document Manager, Editor | Where the older settings file is
 | | looked for (default .config in the home directory); read only to
 | | take settings over when the file config is missing
 | | ({n:appcfg-legacy}).
{c:XDG_CACHE_HOME} | Editor | The directory for the cache of the pictures made
 | | for equations and pictures of the screen (the value must be an
 | | absolute path); the default is .cache in the home directory.
{c:TMPDIR} | Printer, Editor, Document Manager | The directory where the
 | | programs make the files that they need while they work, instead
 | | of the system directory for such files.
{c:PATH} | none | Not read.  The programs of the system are looked for in fixed
 | | directories and never in {c:PATH} ({n:appcmd-find}).  A program that the
 | | Printer starts gets a {c:PATH} of its own: its directory and the system
 | | directories.
{c:DISPLAY} | X11 version, Editor | The X server of the X11 programs.  Preview
 | | checks that it or {c:WAYLAND_DISPLAY} is set when it starts the
 | | Viewer.  The terminal version does not use it.
{c:WAYLAND_DISPLAY} | Editor | Counts as a display for Preview, as {c:DISPLAY}
 | | does.
{c:USER} | Editor | The author name of a new Comment marker.
{c:TERM} | Terminal version | The kind of the terminal: the number of colors and
 | | the test for a multiplexer ({n:appterm-term}).
{c:COLORTERM} | Terminal version | truecolor or 24bit means that the terminal
 | | shows every color ({n:appterm-colour}).
{c:LC_ALL}, {c:LC_CTYPE}, {c:LANG} | Terminal version | The name of the locale, the first
 | | that is set.  In a multiplexer a name with UTF-8 selects UTF-8
 | | characters ({n:appterm-charset}).
.end
.if .STRATA_BUILD_TYPE # release
.h3 Environment variables of the X11 window [appcmd-env-x11]
.ix STRATA_X11_XFT
.ix STRATA_X11_SIZE
.ix STRATA_X11_FONT
.ix STRATA_X11_GEOM
These are read by the X11 version of the Document Manager and of the Editor
only; the terminal version ignores them.  They are described in {n:appx11}.
.table 20 40
Name | Effect
{c:STRATA_X11_XFT} | 0 turns the outline fonts off; unset, empty or 1 uses
 | "DejaVu Sans Mono"; any other value is the family name.
{c:STRATA_X11_SIZE} | The pixel size of the font (default 16 with Xft, 15 with
 | the bitmap fonts; values under 8 give 16 with Xft).
{c:STRATA_X11_FONT} | An X font name for the bitmap font (normal; the bold is
 | made by changing "medium" to "bold" in the name).
{c:STRATA_X11_GEOM} | COLSxROWS, the size of the window in cells (default
 | 80x50; the least is 20 columns and 20 rows).
.end
.endif
.h2 Programs that Strata runs [appcmd-external]
.ix External programs
.ix TeX installation
.ix Prerequisites
Several features need programs that are not part of Strata.  They are all
looked for in fixed directories of the system and never in {c:PATH}
({n:appcmd-find}).  A
missing program disables only the feature that needs it; the Editor,
the Document Manager and the text output work with none of them.
.table 13 18 27
Program | Used by | For
{c:pdflatex} | Printer, Editor | The PDF; the pictures, keycaps and LaTeX markers of
 | | the screen.
{c:latex} | Printer, Editor | The pages of a Preview; the equations.
{c:dvipdfmx} | Printer | A second way to make the PDF.
{c:gs} | Printer | Converting a PDF or EPS picture.
{c:extractbb} | Printer | The size of a picture for a Preview.
{c:kpsewhich} | Editor, Viewer, Document Manager | TeX files, fonts, the font
 | | directory, the test for an installed font.
{c:dvipng} | Editor | The images of equations on the screen.
{c:pdftoppm} | Editor | The images of pictures, keycaps and LaTeX markers on the
 | | screen.
{c:pdfinfo} | Viewer | The size of a PDF picture.
{c:lp} | Editor | Sending the PDF to the printer.
{c:lpstat} | Editor | The list of queues.
{c:aspell}, {c:hunspell} | Editor | The spell check (the first that is found).
{c:curl} | Document Manager | Downloading a font archive.
{c:unzip} | Document Manager | Unpacking it.
{c:mktexlsr} | Document Manager | Updating the TeX file lists after the install.
{c:updmap-user} | Document Manager | Enabling the map file of an installed font.
.end
The equation images are made only when both {c:latex} and {c:dvipng} are in
the system directories, and
the pictures, keycaps and LaTeX markers only when {c:pdflatex} and
{c:pdftoppm} are; otherwise these markers are shown in their Short form on the
screen ({n:markers-screen}, {n:equations}).
.h3 Where each program is looked for [appcmd-find]
.ix Search for programs
.ix Program search order
.table 15 45
Looking for | Order of the search
The Editor (by the Document Manager) | The setting of the Editor program;
 | the Editor in the directory of the Document Manager; the Editor in the
 | system directories.  See {x:str-find-editor}.
The Printer, the Viewer | (by the Editor) The file of that name in the
 | directory of the Editor; otherwise the system directories.
The TeX engines, {c:gs}, {c:lp} and the others | The system directories.
The system directories | {c:/usr/bin}, {c:/bin}, {c:/usr/local/bin}, {c:/usr/sbin},
 | and the directories {c:/usr/local/texlive/YEAR/bin/SYSTEM} of a TeX Live
 | installation, the newest year first.  A program is started only if its
 | file is not writable by its group or by others, belongs to you or to
 | root, and is in a directory that others cannot write to.
Templates | The Working Directory; the environment variable
 | {c:STRATA_TEMPLATES}; the directory of the program.
.end
.h2 Files [appcmd-files]
.ix Files used by the programs
.ix Cache directory
.table 13 47
File | Use
config | In the settings directory.  The settings (read at start by the
 | Document Manager and the Editor; written by Setup and by the Options
 | panel).
fonts | In the settings directory.  The list of fonts for printing (TeX Font
 | Association).
dictionary | In the settings directory.  The personal word list of the spell
 | check ({n:spell}).
The cache | The directory strata under the cache directory of the user (see
 | {c:XDG_CACHE_HOME}): images of equations and pictures.
{c:DOCUMENT.doc} | The document.  Autosave saves a changed document to its own
 | file at the interval of the settings; it needs a file name.
.end
The settings directory and its files are made for the owner only and are
used only if they belong to the user who runs the program.  The complete
list and the format are in {n:appcfg}.
